---
// How to install, as a lesson: the README's eight steps with its real screenshots, a step list that follows the
// scroll (scripts/ui.ts), and the other ways in (32-bit, Scoop, Linux) in tabs. Then the checksums.
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import InstallTabs from '../islands/InstallTabs.tsx';
import { DOWNLOAD_X64, DOWNLOAD_X86, EXTENSION_ZIP, REPO, SUMS, checksums, installSteps, linux, scoop } from '../lib/content';
import { formatMB, latestRelease } from '../lib/release';

const { sizes } = await latestRelease();
const images = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>('../../../docs/images/*.{png,jpg}', { eager: true });
const image = (name: string) => Object.entries(images).find(([k]) => k.endsWith(`/${name}.png`) || k.endsWith(`/${name}.jpg`))![1].default;
const pad = (n: number) => String(n).padStart(2, '0');
---
<section class="section" id="install" aria-labelledby="in-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="counter">011</span>
      <h2 id="in-h">How to install.</h2>
      <p class="lede">{installSteps.length} steps, no administrator rights. The installer already contains the browser extension.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="defer">
    <InstallTabs client:visible>
      <div slot="x64" class="lesson">
        <nav class="lesson-index" aria-label="Steps">
          <p class="label">{installSteps.length} steps</p>
          <ol data-steps-index>
            {installSteps.map((s, i) => <li><a href={`#step-${i + 1}`} data-step-link={i + 1}><span class="mono">{pad(i + 1)}</span>{s.title}</a></li>)}
          </ol>
        </nav>
        <ol class="lesson-steps">
          {installSteps.map((s, i) => (
            <li class="step" id={`step-${i + 1}`} data-step={i + 1}>
              <p class="label step-count">Step <span class="mono">{pad(i + 1)}</span> of <span class="mono">{pad(installSteps.length)}</span></p>
              <h3>{s.title}</h3>
              {s.body.map((p) => <p class="step-text">{p}</p>)}
              {s.list && <ol class="step-list">{s.list.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ol>}
              {s.illustration === 'download' && (
                <div class="dl-card">
                  <span class="file-ico"><Icon name="download" size={22} /></span>
                  <span class="file"><b class="mono">YTDownloadManager-Setup-x64.exe</b>{sizes.x64 && <span class="mono">{formatMB(sizes.x64)}</span>}</span>
                  <a class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" href={DOWNLOAD_X64} data-download>Download<span class="done" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5" /></svg></span></a>
                </div>
              )}
              {s.illustration === 'smartscreen' && (
                <figure class="smartscreen">
                  <div class="ss-box" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of the warning: Windows protected your PC, with More info and then Run anyway">
                    <p class="ss-title">Windows protected your PC</p>
                    <p class="ss-text">Microsoft Defender SmartScreen prevented an unrecognized app from starting. Running this app might put your PC at risk.</p>
                    <p class="ss-more"><span class="ss-link">More info</span></p>
                    <div class="ss-actions"><span class="ss-btn ss-run">Run anyway</span><span class="ss-btn">Don't run</span></div>
                  </div>
                  <figcaption class="caption">Illustration. Click <b>More info</b>, then <b>Run anyway</b>.</figcaption>
                </figure>
              )}
              {s.shot && (
                <figure class="step-shot">
                  <Picture src={image(s.shot.src)} alt={s.shot.alt} formats={['avif', 'webp']} widths={[Math.min(422, image(s.shot.src).width), Math.min(989, image(s.shot.src).width), image(s.shot.src).width].filter((v, j, a) => a.indexOf(v) === j)} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 720px, 100vw" loading="lazy" />
                </figure>
              )}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div slot="x86" class="alt">
        <p>The steps are the same as for Windows 64-bit. The only difference is the file in step 1: download <a href={DOWNLOAD_X86}>YTDownloadManager-Setup-x86.exe</a>{sizes.x86 && <> ({formatMB(sizes.x86)})</>} instead. The windows look exactly the same.</p>
        <p class="hint"><b>Not sure if your Windows is 64-bit or 32-bit?</b> Press the Windows key, type <kbd>About your PC</kbd> and open it. Look at <b>System type</b>. If it says "64-bit operating system", take the 64-bit file. Almost all PCs from the last 10 years are 64-bit.</p>
      </div>

      <div slot="scoop" class="alt">
        <p>If you use <a href="https://scoop.sh">Scoop</a>, open PowerShell and run:</p>
        <div class="codes">
          {scoop.commands.map((c) => (
            <div class="codeblock"><code>{c}</code><button class="copy" type="button" data-copy={c} aria-label={`Copy: ${c}`}>
              <span class="idle"><Icon name="copy" size={16} /></span><span class="ok"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5" /></svg></span><span class="sr-only" data-copy-status></span>
            </button></div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p>{scoop.after}</p>
      </div>

      <div slot="linux" class="alt">
        <p>{linux.intro}</p>
        <ol class="step-list">
          {linux.steps.map((x, i) => <li>{i === 0 ? <>Download <a href={EXTENSION_ZIP}>YTStandaloneDownloader-Extension.zip</a> and unzip it into a folder you keep (for example <code>~/yt-extension</code>).</> : x}</li>)}
        </ol>
        <p class="hint">Browsers from Snap or Flatpak can only open some folders:</p>
        <ul class="step-list">{linux.sandboxes.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
        <p class="hint">{linux.caveat} The <a href={`${REPO}#linux`}>Linux guide</a> in the README has the details.</p>
      </div>
    </InstallTabs>
    </div>

    <div class="sums" id="checksums">
      <div class="sums-text">
        <h3>{checksums.title}</h3>
        <p>{checksums.text}</p>
        <p>Every release ships <a href={SUMS}>SHA256SUMS.txt</a> with the SHA-256 checksum of each of its files. To check a download, compare its checksum with the one listed for that file.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="codes">
        {checksums.commands.map((c) => (
          <div>
            <p class="label">{c.label}</p>
            <div class="codeblock"><code>{c.command}</code><button class="copy" type="button" data-copy={c.command} aria-label={`Copy the ${c.label} command`}>
              <span class="idle"><Icon name="copy" size={16} /></span><span class="ok"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5" /></svg></span><span class="sr-only" data-copy-status></span>
            </button></div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="caption full-guide">Step-by-step pictures, updating and uninstalling are explained in the <a href={`${REPO}#installation`}>full guide</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  :global(.itabs-list) { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); margin-bottom: 40px; }
  :global(.itabs-trigger) { position: relative; height: 48px; padding: 0 16px; border: 0; background: none; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 1rem; cursor: pointer; scroll-margin-top: 120px; }
  :global(.itabs-trigger:hover) { color: var(--ink); }
  :global(.itabs-trigger[data-state="active"]) { color: var(--ink); }
  :global(.itabs-trigger[data-state="active"])::after { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 16px; right: 16px; bottom: -1px; height: 2px; background: var(--tape); }
  :global(.itabs-panel[hidden]) { display: none; }
  .lesson { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr)); column-gap: clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 32px); }
  .lesson-index { grid-column: 1 / span 3; position: sticky; top: 112px; align-self: start; }
  .lesson-index ol { list-style: none; margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .lesson-index a { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.35; transition: color 0.2s var(--ease-tape); }
  .lesson-index a .mono { font-size: 0.75rem; padding-top: 2px; }
  .lesson-index a:hover, .lesson-index a[aria-current="step"] { color: var(--ink); }
  .lesson-index a[aria-current="step"] .mono { color: var(--tape-text); }
  .lesson-steps { grid-column: 5 / span 8; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: clamp(56px, 8vw, 104px); }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) { .lesson-index { display: none; } .lesson-steps { grid-column: 1 / -1; } }
  .step { display: grid; gap: 14px; scroll-margin-top: 110px; }
  .step h3 { font-size: clamp(1.625rem, 1.2rem + 1.2vw, 2.25rem); }
  .step-count .mono { color: var(--ink); letter-spacing: 0; }
  .step-text { color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 60ch; }
  .step-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.3em; display: grid; gap: 8px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 64ch; }
  .step-list li::marker { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--ink-3); }
  .step-shot { margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .step-shot :global(img) { width: auto; max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--radius-md); border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--panel); }
  .dl-card { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin-top: 8px; padding: 14px 14px 14px 16px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--panel); max-width: 560px; }
  .file-ico { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--raise); color: var(--ink-2); }
  .file { flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: grid; gap: 2px; font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  .file b { font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .file span { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .smartscreen { margin: 10px 0 0; max-width: 560px; }
  .ss-box { padding: 26px 26px 20px; background: #1f5ea8; color: #fff; border-radius: 4px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; }
  .ss-title { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .ss-text { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.5; opacity: 0.92; }
  .ss-more { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .ss-link { text-decoration: underline; }
  .ss-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: 8px; margin-top: 26px; }
  .ss-btn { padding: 7px 18px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  .ss-run { outline: 2px solid var(--label); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .smartscreen .caption { margin-top: 10px; }
  .alt { display: grid; gap: 18px; max-width: 72ch; }
  .alt p { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .alt p a, .alt p b { color: var(--ink); }
  .hint { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  kbd { padding: 1px 6px; border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); font-size: 0.85em; }
  .codes { display: grid; gap: 12px; min-width: 0; }
  .codes > * { min-width: 0; }
  .codes .label { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .sums { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr)); column-gap: clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 32px); row-gap: 24px; margin-top: clamp(72px, 10vw, 128px); padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .sums-text { grid-column: 1 / span 5; display: grid; gap: 12px; align-content: start; }
  .sums-text h3 { font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 1.1rem + 0.8vw, 1.75rem); }
  .sums-text p { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.9688rem; }
  .sums-text a { color: var(--ink); }
  .sums .codes { grid-column: 7 / span 6; }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) { .sums-text, .sums .codes { grid-column: 1 / -1; } }
  .full-guide { margin-top: 28px; }
</style>
